      "id": 200,
      "text": "With total ownership, but it absolutely demands an understanding of the underlying mechanics to stay safe. It does. And"
    },
    {
      "id": 201,
      "text": "I want to leave you, the listener, with a final thought today, something to ponder that builds on everything we've learned. Oh, OK."
    },
    {
      "id": 202,
      "text": "So, we established that Bitcoin has a hard limit, right? And that 99% of all coins will be issued by the year 2035."
    },
    {
      "id": 203,
      "text": "Right. We talked about that. We also know that the miners are currently incentivized to burn all that computing power because they receive"
    },
    {
      "id": 204,
      "text": "both newly created coins and transaction fees. Yes. So, what happens decades from now when"
    },
    {
      "id": 205,
      "text": "the block reward drops to absolutely zero and this massive global network of supercomputers has to survive"
    },
    {
      "id": 206,
      "text": "entirely on the transaction fees from users alone? Will the incentive structure hold up? Will the network remain secure?"
    },
    {
      "id": 207,
      "text": "It is arguably the most profound open question in the entire field of cryptocurrency engineering. It really"
    },
    {
      "id": 208,
      "text": "makes you rethink the mechanics of value. Well, thank you for joining us on this deep dive. Keep questioning, keep learning, and remember,"
    },
    {
      "id": 209,
      "text": "whether it's a physical 20 bill in your... The real currency"
    },
    {
      "id": 210,
      "text": "is trust. See you next time."
    }
  ]
}
